# Build context for infra/docker/server.Dockerfile. The context is the repository root, and
# BuildKit reads this file — `<dockerfile>.dockerignore`, next to the Dockerfile — in preference to
# a context-level `.dockerignore`, which is why the rules live here with the Dockerfile they serve
# instead of in a root file shared with builds that do not exist.
#
# Stage `prune` does `COPY . .`, so everything not excluded here is uploaded and hashed on every
# build. Two rules must never be relaxed: `pnpm-lock.yaml` and `pnpm-workspace.yaml` are what make
# the pruned install reproducible, and every workspace `package.json` is what `turbo prune` reads.

# Installed and generated trees: the image installs from the lockfile and builds from source.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.vitest
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and release output.
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
apps/desktop/release
apps/e2e/.auth
tooling/mutation/reports

# Repository metadata and local files that never affect the image.
.git
.github
.changeset
.vscode
.idea
docs
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
**/*.local
**/.env
**/.env.*
